# Patch: publish each hunk's start line where the diff card can read it
#
# WHICH PATCH: this is "patch 2 of 2" — the rendering half. It pairs with
# patches/dsh-tool-fs-hunk-lines.patch: that one puts oldStart/newStart into meta.diffs, this
# one attaches them to the DOM. Applied alone it publishes nothing (there are no numbers yet).
#
# APPLIES TO: the SHIPPED, MINIFIED Vite bundle inside the Electron asar.
#   dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-frontend/dist/assets/index-CN7NIWNw.js
#   (@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-frontend 0.2.1-rc.2)
# Archive-relative like the other patch; apply from a mirror of the asar root, never at the
# installation. Use tools/patch-asar.mjs for the real thing.
#
# *** FRAGILITY: HIGH. READ THIS BEFORE UPDATING THE APP. ***
# Unlike the lib/ patches, this targets a MINIFIED bundle: 192 lines, the largest 193,231
# characters, all identifiers renamed to one or two letters. The three anchors below are exact
# byte matches against the build named above. A rebuild — even a patch release with no relevant
# source change — will very likely rename or merge X_/gF/yF, and then this patch will refuse to
# apply. That is a designed, safe failure: tools/patch-asar.mjs reports the patch as SKIPPED,
# leaves it out, and still installs patch 1 (which is harmless on its own). Re-derive the
# anchors against the new bundle before reusing this file.
#
# WHY an attribute instead of a row field:
#   The row shape is {kind, text} — the renderer spreads a fixed {className, children} and
#   nothing downstream reads a start/lineNumber field, so channel (a) had nowhere to attach.
#   The attributes are written on the FIRST ROW of each hunk, not on the body, because
#   cds-theme's diffnumbers.js numbers a card in body mode only when it has ONE contiguous
#   segment: any multi-hunk card has the ⋯ separator and is numbered in row mode, which
#   requires every segment's first row to declare its own start. A body-level attribute would
#   light up single-hunk cards and leave multi-hunk ones at 1..n — the case users notice.
#
# WHY the start is computed as i.newStart + s.newStart - 1:
#   i is the meta hunk carrying patch 1's numbers; X_(i) re-diffs that hunk's own texts, and
#   because those texts are already a slice of the file, jsdiff numbers the result from 1. So
#   the sub-hunk's file line is the hunk's file start plus the sub-hunk's own line minus one.
#   Nothing is recomputed from the file: patch 1's numbers stay the only source of truth.
#   When i.newStart is absent (a session recorded before patch 1) no attribute is written at
#   all, so the theme keeps counting 1..n instead of printing a confidently wrong number.

